Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.56,0:00:04.03,White-Standard,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(1150,500)}Tuldarr Academy of Magic
Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.91,0:00:09.90,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,An interesting idea, creating \Nan academy for the children of mages.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.34,0:00:13.36,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,How many students would you say \Nare currently enrolled?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:13.64,0:00:17.07,Default,Headmaster,0,0,0,,Fifty-two children are here \Nto learn to control their magic,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:17.07,0:00:20.79,Default,Headmaster,0,0,0,,and sixty-eight students are\Nstudying to become mages.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.18,0:00:24.75,Default,Headmaster,0,0,0,,Half the children will remain \Nat the academy to become mages,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.06,0:00:28.46,Default,Headmaster,0,0,0,,and even less will become \Nappointed as royal mages.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:29.51,0:00:32.75,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,The future of Tuldarr rests in their hands.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:33.55,0:00:37.01,Default,Headmaster,0,0,0,,In addition, word got out that \NYour Majesty will be giving a lesson,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.53,0:00:41.35,Default,Headmaster,0,0,0,,so there are a number of children \Nfrom town who want to sit in.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:41.65,0:00:43.48,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I don't mind at all.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:43.48,0:00:45.94,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Please let anyone interested take part.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:45.94,0:00:47.98,Default,Headmaster,0,0,0,,Thank you very much, Your Majesty.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:53.98,0:00:55.45,Default,Renart,0,0,0,,Queen Tinasha!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:55.45,0:00:56.32,Default,Headmaster,0,0,0,,What's this?!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:56.78,0:00:57.68,Default,Renart,0,0,0,,Are you unhurt?!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:57.68,0:00:59.30,Default,Teacher A,0,0,0,,The building's collapsed!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:01.10,0:01:02.90,Default,Teacher B,0,0,0,,The children are trapped underneath!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:02.90,0:01:04.16,Default,Teacher A,0,0,0,,Call the medics!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:06.06,0:01:07.84,Default,Headmaster,0,0,0,,Step away from the building!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:07.84,0:01:10.67,Default,Headmaster,0,0,0,,Those who can help, rescue \Nthe injured and administer first aid!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:23.62,0:01:26.06,Default,Woman,0,0,0,,Is that really my son?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:27.18,0:01:29.67,Default,Woman,0,0,0,,If only it had been me instead...
Dialogue: 0,0:01:33.81,0:01:36.48,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,{\i1}You cannot change events \Nthat have come to pass.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:37.07,0:01:39.12,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,{\i1}Magic can't fix everything.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:40.21,0:01:44.46,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,{\i1}You can stop time, but turning it back isn't...
Dialogue: 0,0:01:48.49,0:01:49.29,Default,Renart,0,0,0,,Your Majesty?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:49.29,0:01:50.61,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Excuse me.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:50.61,0:01:52.25,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I leave the rest to you.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:53.16,0:01:54.00,Default,Renart,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:01.89,0:02:05.00,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Be unsealed and show your true form!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:49.17,0:03:54.00,Ep Title,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(500,1)}~ Bloodless Scars ~
Dialogue: 0,0:03:54.98,0:03:59.83,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,You're saying you used it for yourself \Nafter all those warnings you gave me?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:00.43,0:04:01.92,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I'm sorry.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:01.92,0:04:04.70,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,I get wanting to save those children,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:04.70,0:04:07.21,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,but you can't use it to go back \Nto the past every time.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:10.41,0:04:15.52,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Well, that's the part of you I like.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:18.34,0:04:20.60,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,So, did you manage to save them?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:22.50,0:04:24.61,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,It didn't activate.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:24.61,0:04:26.69,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,It didn't?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:26.69,0:04:27.96,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Does that mean it's broken?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:29.81,0:04:32.95,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,There may be conditions needed to activate it.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:37.72,0:04:38.94,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I'm sorry.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:39.72,0:04:42.03,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,You can stay here until tomorrow morning.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:43.13,0:04:44.80,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,No, I'll be leaving.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:47.19,0:04:48.54,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,That reminds me.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:49.07,0:04:51.77,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,It seems there's turmoil within Cezar.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:52.79,0:04:55.56,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Some people have been taken \Nto their castle, never to return,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:55.56,0:04:58.81,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,and many others have gone missing as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:59.53,0:05:01.40,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,I see. I'll be careful.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:02.89,0:05:04.68,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I'll be going now.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:06.03,0:05:06.91,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Um...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:07.88,0:05:09.70,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Thank you very much.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:11.23,0:05:12.84,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Feel free to drop by anytime.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:23.83,0:05:26.35,Default-Top,Cezar Mage A,0,0,0,,Valt. Isn't it about time?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:25.42,0:05:28.51,White-Standard,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(900,1)}Cezar Military Camp
Dialogue: 0,0:05:26.35,0:05:29.52,Default-Top,Cezar Mage A,0,0,0,,If we leave it alone any longer, \Nit may very well devour us, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:29.98,0:05:31.25,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,I suppose.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:31.25,0:05:32.77,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,Sounds good to me.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:33.07,0:05:35.79,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,I'll handle things until it emerges here,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:36.50,0:05:38.76,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,since no one else here is capable.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:39.31,0:05:41.50,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,You can do as you like after that.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:41.50,0:05:43.26,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,Don't expect me to control it.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:43.69,0:05:44.68,Default,Cezar Mage A,0,0,0,,That's fine.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:44.68,0:05:46.22,Default,Cezar Mage A,0,0,0,,We'll deal with it on our own.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:51.41,0:05:54.75,White-Standard,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(1150,500)}Ynureid Fortress    {\fs14}Northwestern Farsas, Bordering Druza
Dialogue: 0,0:05:53.87,0:05:56.16,Default-Top,Oscar,0,0,0,,So Cezar has made their move.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:56.54,0:05:57.90,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,How's it look?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:57.90,0:06:00.88,Default,General,0,0,0,,Most of their men are on foot, \Nso they're advancing slowly.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:00.88,0:06:04.50,Default,General,0,0,0,,It'll be some time before they arrive here.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:04.97,0:06:05.94,Default,General,0,0,0,,However...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:06.61,0:06:07.72,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,What's wrong?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:07.72,0:06:11.34,Default,General,0,0,0,,Our mages say they can sense \Na strange magical power.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:13.62,0:06:16.77,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,They all know they can't win \Nin a head-on fight,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:16.77,0:06:18.87,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,so they keep trying to pull these weird tricks.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:20.11,0:06:21.77,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Let's take a gamble here.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:28.20,0:06:31.20,White-Standard,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(1,500)\pos(415,290)}Tarvo    {\fs14}Cezar General
Dialogue: 0,0:06:28.58,0:06:31.20,Default-Top,Tarvo,0,0,0,,Looks like Farsas hasn't caught on yet.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:33.00,0:06:36.54,Default,Tarvo,0,0,0,,Looking at Druza's tactics, \Nit's little wonder they were defeated.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:36.54,0:06:39.26,Default,Tarvo,0,0,0,,A forbidden curse to destroy \Nstrongholds and troops is one thing,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:39.26,0:06:42.26,Default,Tarvo,0,0,0,,but what were they planning to do \Nonce that was exhausted?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:42.63,0:06:45.83,Default,Cezar Lt. Gen.,0,0,0,,Cezar won't repeat their mistakes.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:45.83,0:06:50.29,Default,Cezar Lt. Gen.,0,0,0,,We've spent many years building \Nour armed forces for this occasion.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:50.29,0:06:52.91,Default,Tarvo,0,0,0,,Not to mention our secret weapon.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:53.35,0:06:56.41,Default,Tarvo,0,0,0,,I don't see a single reason why we would lose.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:00.89,0:07:01.64,Default,Tarvo,0,0,0,,What?!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:01.64,0:07:03.12,Default,Tarvo,0,0,0,,What's happening here?!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:06.71,0:07:10.03,Default,Tarvo,0,0,0,,Our marching soldiers are all safe, I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:10.03,0:07:12.64,Default,Cezar Lt. Gen.,0,0,0,,General Tarvo, what should we do?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:12.64,0:07:14.60,Default,Tarvo,0,0,0,,It's of no matter. Proceed onward.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:14.60,0:07:15.27,Default,Cezar Lt. Gen.,0,0,0,,Yes!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:21.85,0:07:24.42,Default,Tarvo,0,0,0,,It seems we have the right route.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:28.09,0:07:29.46,Default,Cezar Lt. Gen.,0,0,0,,G-General!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:36.41,0:07:41.27,Default,Kav,0,0,0,,This spell Queen Tinasha taught us \Nto cover flat ground in fog...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:41.65,0:07:43.41,Default,Kav,0,0,0,,It's really strong.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:43.41,0:07:48.51,Default,Sylvia,0,0,0,,This is spirit magic, so regular mages \Nwould normally be unable to cast it.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:48.51,0:07:53.58,Default,Kav,0,0,0,,Yet she came up with a new \Ncomposition that lets us use it.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:53.58,0:07:55.70,Default,Kav,0,0,0,,She really is something else.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:58.67,0:08:00.50,Default,Sylvia,0,0,0,,I just hope nothing goes wrong.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:01.00,0:08:04.26,Default,Sylvia,0,0,0,,If only Queen Tinasha could be here right now.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:14.18,0:08:16.18,Default,Als,0,0,0,,Th-They're...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:24.90,0:08:27.45,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,So this is what they meant \Nby strange magical power?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:30.28,0:08:34.71,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Taken to Cezar's castle, never to return, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:35.11,0:08:36.22,Default,Doan,0,0,0,,Your Majesty!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:36.22,0:08:37.08,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,I know.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:37.08,0:08:38.86,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,We'll have to engage them with magic.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:38.86,0:08:40.59,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Not my style, but let's do it!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:41.10,0:08:42.08,Default,Doan,0,0,0,,Mage squad!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:42.08,0:08:43.32,Default,Doan,0,0,0,,Ready!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:44.36,0:08:45.41,Default,Doan,0,0,0,,Fire!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:07.49,0:09:08.90,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,There's no end to them...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:10.21,0:09:11.47,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,That's it, Doan.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:11.47,0:09:11.94,Default,Doan,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:12.99,0:09:15.10,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Aim that at me and fire.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:15.90,0:09:16.98,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Hurry up.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:16.98,0:09:18.81,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,When you do, Tinasha will take notice.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:18.81,0:09:20.34,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,This is our last resort.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:21.75,0:09:24.71,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Please don't summon me like that.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:34.23,0:09:36.28,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,You sure like to make a scene.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:38.30,0:09:41.36,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I was hoping to get a chance to speak with you.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:47.00,0:09:52.90,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I am the queen of Tuldarr, \NTinasha As Meyer Ur Aeterna Tuldarr.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:53.64,0:09:58.44,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,We have detected the use of \Nforbidden magic in this war.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:58.44,0:10:02.89,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,As such, Tuldarr has taken it \Nupon ourselves to intervene.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:02.89,0:10:07.10,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Please understand that we act here \Nto eliminate what should not exist,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:07.10,0:10:10.98,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,and not in the interest \Nof either party concerned.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:10.98,0:10:12.49,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Understood.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:12.49,0:10:14.50,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Thanks for acting so quickly.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:15.73,0:10:18.46,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I'll be leaving two spirits with you,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:18.46,0:10:20.30,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,as well as them.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:20.95,0:10:23.64,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I'm planning to have them serve \Nas an anti-forbidden-curse unit,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:23.64,0:10:25.39,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,so please work them hard.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:26.05,0:10:28.14,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Tuldarr mages?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:28.14,0:10:30.77,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,I suppose we don't know much \Nabout forbidden curses.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:30.77,0:10:31.62,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Thanks.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:32.90,0:10:38.18,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,That said, they're still trainees who \Nhaven't faced any real forbidden curses yet.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:38.18,0:10:40.61,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,They {\i1}are{\i0} excellent mages, though.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:40.90,0:10:44.33,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Now I'm not sure what I should think of them.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:44.69,0:10:48.40,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I'm off to go dispatch Simila, \Nthe cause of these corpses.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:48.40,0:10:49.74,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Simila?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:49.74,0:10:52.54,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,I remember that name \Nfrom when you got poisoned.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:52.54,0:10:56.43,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,It's the god worshiped \Nby the weird cult from back then.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:56.43,0:11:00.73,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Or rather, it's an evil god told of \Nsince ancient times in Cezar.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:00.73,0:11:01.81,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Evil god?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:01.81,0:11:03.23,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,What's this about an evil god?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:03.23,0:11:05.18,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Don't tell me those really exist.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:05.80,0:11:10.39,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Well, I don't think it really dates back \Nto mythological times, like Aetea.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:10.98,0:11:15.76,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Still, it's some sort of accumulation \Nof magic and souls.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:15.76,0:11:17.48,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I should be fit to handle it.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:17.48,0:11:20.65,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,If it's too much for you, \Njust wait and I'll be right there.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:20.65,0:11:21.94,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I'll be fine.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:24.29,0:11:26.04,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,You're sure you can win, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:26.04,0:11:26.74,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Of course.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:27.73,0:11:30.27,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Make sure you come back alive.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:32.33,0:11:33.82,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Leave it to me.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:33.82,0:11:36.41,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I'll be awaiting your return in the fortress.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:38.51,0:11:39.97,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,O-Oscar!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:40.53,0:11:43.25,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,W-We're in the middle of a battle!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:43.25,0:11:45.43,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Yeah. Go on now.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:47.34,0:11:48.96,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Senn. Lilia.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:48.96,0:11:50.59,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I leave this in your hands.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:50.59,0:11:51.54,Default,Senn,0,0,0,,Yes, my lady.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:51.54,0:11:52.84,Default,Lilia,0,0,0,,As you wish.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:53.98,0:11:55.86,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Best of luck out there.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:56.18,0:11:57.19,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,You too.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:02.99,0:12:05.03,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Okay, let's go.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:12.43,0:12:15.15,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,That... sure is something.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:15.50,0:12:18.50,White-Standard,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(1,500)}Simila    {\fs14}Evil God
Dialogue: 0,0:12:17.53,0:12:19.88,Default-Top,Tinasha,0,0,0,,It's so gross-looking...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:20.97,0:12:23.72,Default,Mila,0,0,0,,Lady Tinasha, you're creeped out by that?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:23.72,0:12:26.14,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I mean, it doesn't have any legs.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:26.14,0:12:27.20,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,{\i1}And{\i0} it's huge.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:27.20,0:12:28.81,Default,Mila,0,0,0,,So you'd be fine if it had legs?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:28.81,0:12:31.08,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,That's not what I mean.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:33.90,0:12:38.09,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I wonder where that's connected to.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:38.72,0:12:40.75,Default,Karr,0,0,0,,Maybe it's a conceptual entity?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:40.75,0:12:45.85,Default,Karr,0,0,0,,If there is a source, I'd imagine this goes \Ndown all the way to the lowest realm.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:45.85,0:12:50.81,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,The evil god itself looks to be composed \Nmostly of magic and human souls.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:50.81,0:12:53.10,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,It's been given form through \Nhuman flesh and blood,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:53.10,0:12:55.85,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,then manifested with a definition, I suppose?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:55.85,0:12:58.75,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,It seems like we're dealing with \Nquite a talented caster.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:59.55,0:13:01.51,Default,Karr,0,0,0,,Can't say much for their taste...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:01.79,0:13:03.05,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,All right.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:03.05,0:13:05.18,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Let's give this a shot.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:08.49,0:13:11.26,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Fly through the night, \Ndespair that has rejected slumber.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:11.26,0:13:12.56,Default,Karr,0,0,0,,Be defined and appear before me.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:12.56,0:13:15.60,Default,Mila,0,0,0,,By my command, \Nrepeat the sequence forevermore.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:17.24,0:13:19.10,Default,Cezar Mage A,0,0,0,,H-Hey! We need a barrier!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:19.10,0:13:19.69,Default,Cezar Mage B,0,0,0,,It's no good!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:19.69,0:13:20.80,Default,Cezar Mage B,0,0,0,,We won't make it!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:43.15,0:13:44.42,Default,Mila,0,0,0,,That thing...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:44.42,0:13:45.67,Default,Karr,0,0,0,,It's absorbing them!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:50.44,0:13:51.95,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Just awful.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:51.95,0:13:53.27,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,How frustrating.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:53.80,0:13:57.09,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,That means makeshift restraints \Nwill do us no good.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:57.09,0:13:58.80,Default,Karr,0,0,0,,What now, little girl?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:02.41,0:14:05.69,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Can you stop the supply of energy \Ncoming from that opening?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:05.69,0:14:07.24,Default,Karr,0,0,0,,Not with just us two.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:07.79,0:14:09.84,Default,Karr,0,0,0,,Maybe if there were five of us here.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:09.84,0:14:11.90,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Let's go with that, then.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:11.90,0:14:13.71,Default,Karr,0,0,0,,Why do you want to cut off its supply?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:15.78,0:14:17.71,Default,Karr,0,0,0,,L-Little girl...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:17.71,0:14:19.79,Default,Karr,0,0,0,,You're not thinking of \Nabsorbing that, are you?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:20.22,0:14:23.79,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Magic doesn't make up \Na large part of its composition.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:23.79,0:14:28.26,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Once it loses the energy it needs to \Nmanifest, it should disintegrate on its own.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:28.26,0:14:30.92,Default,Karr,0,0,0,,Theoretically, sure...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:30.92,0:14:34.91,Default,Karr,0,0,0,,But what if you absorb too much \Nmagic and destroy your body?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:34.91,0:14:37.73,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I'll release the magic \Nif things start to look bad.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:39.38,0:14:42.19,Default,Karr,0,0,0,,That's our only option, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:43.58,0:14:45.86,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Eir. Nil. Sylpha.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:52.18,0:14:54.26,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Okay, here we go.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:01.29,0:15:02.64,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,That's amazing.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:03.23,0:15:06.09,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Was it like this against Tayiri \Nfour hundred years ago?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:06.09,0:15:07.46,Default,Lilia,0,0,0,,Not exactly.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:07.76,0:15:10.76,Default,Lilia,0,0,0,,These corpses move a lot slower, \Nand they burn more easily.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:10.76,0:15:12.64,Default,Lilia,0,0,0,,It's a lot easier than back then.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:13.49,0:15:16.29,Default,Lilia,0,0,0,,We don't have that many \Nmages in Tuldarr, either.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:16.29,0:15:18.93,Default,Lilia,0,0,0,,Soldiers on horseback would be hard to handle.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:18.93,0:15:20.33,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:28.47,0:15:31.53,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,The annoying part is that \NI can't tell when it'll end.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:31.53,0:15:32.46,Default,Als,0,0,0,,Your Majesty!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:33.29,0:15:40.08,Default,Als,0,0,0,,It seems Cezar has long been controlled \Nby Simila and the cult that worships it.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:40.08,0:15:42.19,Default,Doan,0,0,0,,The current king obeys \Nevery whim of the cult leader,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:42.19,0:15:45.04,Default,Doan,0,0,0,,and all the people \Nwho oppose his policies are killed.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:49.53,0:15:52.80,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,To join their army of immortal soldiers, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:57.43,0:15:59.39,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Let's get started.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:07.62,0:16:09.48,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Keep your eyes on me.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:10.00,0:16:13.95,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I am the first and last despair you will face.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:14.42,0:16:15.48,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Come.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:15.48,0:16:16.78,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Let us dance.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:45.05,0:16:46.29,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Be dispersed.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:52.60,0:16:53.95,Default,Mila,0,0,0,,Is it over?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:55.48,0:16:56.41,Default,Karr,0,0,0,,No!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:57.53,0:16:59.12,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Th-The pain...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:08.77,0:17:09.92,Default,Mila,0,0,0,,Lady Tinasha!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:09.92,0:17:12.14,Default,Karr,0,0,0,,Mila! Don't break formation!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:12.14,0:17:13.09,Default,Mila,0,0,0,,Karr!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:13.09,0:17:14.75,Default,Mila,0,0,0,,We need to tear that thing off, right now!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:14.75,0:17:16.80,Default,Mila,0,0,0,,It'll use the magic \Nshe absorbed to take control!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:16.80,0:17:20.29,Default,Karr,0,0,0,,If you abandon the spell, \Nwe'll lose all our chance of victory!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:20.29,0:17:21.97,Default,Karr,0,0,0,,Have a little more faith in her!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:36.97,0:17:41.60,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,{\i1}There's more to the world \Nthan what we can observe.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:43.32,0:17:49.29,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,{\i1}Untold numbers of invisible layers \Non top of one another.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:49.99,0:17:53.08,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,{\i1}We refer to these as "planes of existence."
Dialogue: 0,0:17:54.52,0:17:57.43,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,{\i1}From heavenly virtues to the negative deep.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:58.07,0:18:01.96,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,{\i1}All of it is contained in this one world.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:03.22,0:18:05.68,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,{\i1}Someone told me that before.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:06.79,0:18:10.24,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,{\i1}Although I can't say what "before" is, exactly.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:10.92,0:18:13.68,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,{\i1}It's very dark here.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:14.33,0:18:15.90,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,{\i1}I can't see a thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:18.86,0:18:21.43,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,{\i1}My name is undefined.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:24.99,0:18:26.31,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,{\i1}Are you waiting?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:45.01,0:18:46.72,Default,Mila,0,0,0,,Lady Tinasha!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:49.90,0:18:51.30,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Ow!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:51.30,0:18:55.32,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I haven't ached this much \Nin four hundred years...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:57.11,0:18:58.46,Default,Karr,0,0,0,,Of course not.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:58.46,0:19:00.11,Default,Karr,0,0,0,,You're saturated with magic.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:00.73,0:19:02.60,Default,Karr,0,0,0,,We'll handle everything else.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:02.60,0:19:04.09,Default,Karr,0,0,0,,You go ahead and rest up.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:05.53,0:19:07.00,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Thanks...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:15.59,0:19:20.22,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Does this mean she's done it?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:20.22,0:19:21.97,Default,Doan,0,0,0,,That seems to be the case!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:22.52,0:19:25.25,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Then let's clean up and get out of here.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:25.25,0:19:25.98,Default,Group,0,0,0,,Yes!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:27.07,0:19:30.01,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,I'm getting sick of seeing all these corpses.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:33.01,0:19:34.94,Default,Sylvia,0,0,0,,How are you feeling?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:35.48,0:19:38.26,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I'll be good as new once I get some sleep.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:38.26,0:19:39.85,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Thanks for your concern.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:39.85,0:19:43.20,Default,Karr,0,0,0,,I'm off to help Mira with the aftermath \Nbefore she snaps at me.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:43.61,0:19:46.41,Default,Karr,0,0,0,,The little lady's in your hands, Miss Mage.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:46.41,0:19:48.09,Default,Sylvia,0,0,0,,You can leave her to me!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:50.70,0:19:52.78,Default,Sylvia,0,0,0,,What happened, exactly?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:52.78,0:19:54.14,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,You see...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:54.98,0:19:57.06,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,My memories are hazy.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:57.06,0:20:01.55,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I was in a strange place \Nwhere I understood everything.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:02.58,0:20:05.01,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,But I can't remember it anymore.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:05.86,0:20:08.05,Default,Sylvia,0,0,0,,That happens a lot with dreams.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:08.05,0:20:10.83,Default,Sylvia,0,0,0,,You start to forget them \Nas soon as you wake up.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:10.83,0:20:13.00,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Yeah, exactly.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:13.60,0:20:18.04,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Still, that should have dealt some \Nserious damage to the Cezar army.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:18.04,0:20:19.94,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Now the corpses are dead.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:20.32,0:20:23.77,Default,Sylvia,0,0,0,,Which means His Majesty \Nshould be returning soon.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:23.77,0:20:25.66,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,I'll have to make this quick, then.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:25.66,0:20:27.87,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,I'd rather not face the wielder of Akashia.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:30.20,0:20:31.29,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Sylvia!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:32.25,0:20:33.21,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,How dare you!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:33.21,0:20:34.92,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,You shouldn't be straining yourself.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:36.84,0:20:39.34,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,You can rest up all you like once we get there.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:40.06,0:20:42.05,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,We still have plenty of time.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:49.97,0:20:52.18,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Tinasha's been kidnapped?!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:52.59,0:20:54.26,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Was it a man with silver hair?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:54.26,0:20:57.15,Default,Kav,0,0,0,,No, it seems she didn't get \Na good look at his face.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:57.15,0:21:00.16,Default,Kav,0,0,0,,He was clad in black mage robes.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:02.97,0:21:04.57,Default,Mila,0,0,0,,Karr! This is {\i1}your{\i0} fault!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:04.57,0:21:07.03,Default,Mila,0,0,0,,Why didn't you stay with Lady Tinasha?!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:08.22,0:21:09.49,Default,Karr,0,0,0,,My bad.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:09.49,0:21:11.04,Default,Mila,0,0,0,,Excuse me?!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:11.87,0:21:14.46,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Tinasha and I are the only ones at fault here.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:14.90,0:21:16.72,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Can you track where she is?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:16.72,0:21:20.67,Default,Karr,0,0,0,,Actually, I can't sense her magic at all.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:21.08,0:21:24.89,Default,Karr,0,0,0,,Either she shut it off herself, \Nor an incredibly powerful seal's been placed.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:25.54,0:21:29.89,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,For both the attempted poisoning and \Nthe Delilah case before Tinasha's coronation,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:29.89,0:21:32.76,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,we received word that \Na male mage was behind it all.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:33.58,0:21:36.22,Default,Doan,0,0,0,,There was a man who matched \Nhis description very closely.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:36.22,0:21:41.30,Default,Doan,0,0,0,,The one who came to Farsas posing as a Yarda \Nroyal mage, only to suddenly disappear.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:41.30,0:21:45.61,Default,Als,0,0,0,,We know it was a Simila worship cult \Nthat sent Delilah to begin with!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:46.95,0:21:49.03,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Valt was behind it all, then...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:55.41,0:21:59.90,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,He was after Tinasha from the very start!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:35.43,0:23:39.98,Next Ep Title,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(500,1)}~ Joyful Sorrow ~
